  "id": "COMPOUND:28526 - PROTEIN:1235",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (1R,3S,4R,7S,8R,12R)-3,8-dihydroxy-4,8,12-trimethyl-15-methylidene-13,18-dioxatricyclo[10.3.2.14,7]octadecane-11,14-dione and Potassium channel subfamily K member 9, as it is identified as a target of multiple cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors. These inhibitors are known to modulate potassium channels, which are critical for cellular excitability and membrane potential regulation. The compound's role as a target of several structurally diverse cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors implies a possible mechanism of action involving the inhibition of potassium channel activity, possibly through direct binding or allosteric modulation. The consistent presence of the compound as a target of multiple inhibitors, coupled with the known involvement of potassium channels in various physiological processes, supports the hypothesis that this compound may interact with potassium channels to exert its effects. The evidence is robust and aligns with established mechanisms of action in the field of potassium channel modulation.",
